@lang en
-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- The computable rules of Parts 1 to 3 of the Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland) that are not about time: the Act's own definitions of "Act", "enactment",
-- "statutory instrument" and "repeal" (s 2(1)); when a provision of the Act applies (s 4); the directions to a court (ss 5 to 7); summary proceedings (s 8);
-- what a reference to a Part or a subsection is read as (s 9); examples (s 11); forms (s 12); judicial notice (s 13); how an Act may be cited (s 14(1)).
-- Rules about periods and commencement are in ie-interpretation-time.l4.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.
-- Most functions answer a question of the form "does this section give X in these circumstances?".
-- FALSE means the section does not give X; it does not mean the section forbids X.
-- A rule that depends on a judgment the Act leaves to the reader (for example whether a provision is "obscure or ambiguous") takes that judgment as an INPUT.
-- Where the text does not say, the function refuses with a named reason.
--
-- Section 4(1) (contrary intention) is dealt with once, in this module, by `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment`;
-- the other functions assume that no contrary intention appears, as ie-interpretation-time.l4 does.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Named refusals`

-- src:90 | “repeal” includes revoke, rescind, abrogate or cancel;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 2(1) "repeal" (src:90)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 2(1) says that repeal includes the listed words, so whether another word is a repeal is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 2(1) says that repeal includes the listed words, so whether another word is a repeal is not answered"

-- src:132 | References in enactments to Parts, etc. 9.—(1) A reference in an enactment to a Part, Chapter, section, Schedule or other division, by whatever name called, shall be read as a reference to a Part, Chapter, section, Schedule or other division of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
-- src:133 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause, article, subarticle or other division, by whatever name called, shall be read as a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause, article, subarticle or other division of the provision in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 9 (src:132-133)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 9 does not say which kind of division a division with another name is` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 9 does not say which kind of division a division with another name is"

-- src:143 | Judicial notice. 13.—An Act is a public document and shall be judicially noticed.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 13 (src:143)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 13 says nothing about a statutory instrument` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 13 says nothing about a statutory instrument"

-- src:119 | Construing provisions in changing circumstances. 6.—In construing a provision of any Act or statutory instrument, a court may make allowances for any changes in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used in that Act or statutory instrument and other relevant matters, which have occurred since the date of the passing of that Act or the making of that statutory instrument, but only in so far as its text, purpose and context permit.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 6 (src:119)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 6 does not say whether a change on the very day of the passing or making is a change since that day` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 6 does not say whether a change on the very day of the passing or making is a change since that day"

§ `Section 2(1): "Act", "statutory instrument" and "enactment"`

DECLARE `Facts about a document` HAS
    `it is an Act of the Oireachtas`                                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a statute that was in force in Saorstat Eireann immediately before the Constitution came into operation`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it continued in force by virtue of Article 50 of the Constitution`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an order, regulation, rule, bye-law, warrant, licence, certificate, direction, notice, guideline or other like document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under an Act or such an instrument`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a portion of an Act or of a statutory instrument`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:86 | “Act” means—
-- src:87 | (a) an Act of the Oireachtas, and
-- src:88 | (b) a statute which was in force in Saorstát Éireann immediately before the date of the coming into operation of the Constitution and which continued in force by virtue of Article 50 of the Constitution;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 2(1) "Act" (src:86-88)
GIVEN doc IS A `Facts about a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an Act` doc MEANS
        doc's `it is an Act of the Oireachtas`
     OR (    doc's `it is a statute that was in force in Saorstat Eireann immediately before the Constitution came into operation`
         AND doc's `it continued in force by virtue of Article 50 of the Constitution`)

-- src:91 | “statutory instrument” means an order, regulation, rule, bye-law, warrant, licence, certificate, direction, notice, guideline or other like document made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under an Act and references, in relation to a statutory instrument, to “made” or to “made under” include references to made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under such instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 2(1) "statutory instrument" (src:91)
GIVEN doc IS A `Facts about a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a statutory instrument` doc MEANS
        doc's `it is an order, regulation, rule, bye-law, warrant, licence, certificate, direction, notice, guideline or other like document`
    AND doc's `it was made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under an Act or such an instrument`

-- src:89 | “enactment” means an Act or a statutory instrument or any portion of an Act or statutory instrument;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 2(1) "enactment" (src:89)
GIVEN doc IS A `Facts about a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an enactment` doc MEANS
        `is an Act` doc
     OR `is a statutory instrument` doc
     OR doc's `it is a portion of an Act or of a statutory instrument`

§ `Section 2(1): "repeal" includes revoke, rescind, abrogate or cancel`

DECLARE `A word for ending an enactment` IS ONE OF
    repeal
    revoke
    rescind
    abrogate
    cancel
    `some other word`

-- src:90 | “repeal” includes revoke, rescind, abrogate or cancel;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 2(1) "repeal" (src:90)
GIVEN w IS A `A word for ending an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the word is a repeal within the Act` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN repeal            THEN TRUE
    WHEN revoke            THEN TRUE
    WHEN rescind           THEN TRUE
    WHEN abrogate          THEN TRUE
    WHEN cancel            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other word` THEN `section 2(1) says that repeal includes the listed words, so whether another word is a repeal is not answered`

§ `Section 4: when a provision of the Act applies`

DECLARE `Where a contrary intention appears` HAS
    `in this Act`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the enactment itself`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Act under which it is made`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:106 | Application. 4.—(1) A provision of this Act applies to an enactment except in so far as the contrary intention appears in this Act, in the enactment itself or, where relevant, in the Act under which the enactment is made.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 4(1) (src:106)
GIVEN where IS A `Where a contrary intention appears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` where MEANS
    NOT (   where's `in this Act`
         OR where's `in the enactment itself`
         OR (CONSIDER where's `in the Act under which it is made`
             WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST flag THEN flag))

-- src:107 | (2) The provisions of this Act which relate to other Acts also apply to this Act unless the contrary intention appears in this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 4(2) (src:107)
GIVEN `the contrary intention appears in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of this Act that relates to other Acts applies also to this Act` `the contrary intention appears in this Act` MEANS
    NOT `the contrary intention appears in this Act`

§ `Section 5: construing a provision that is obscure, ambiguous or absurd`

DECLARE `Whose plain intention` IS ONE OF
    `the Oireachtas`
    `the parliament concerned`
    `the maker of the instrument`

DECLARE `What section 5 directs` IS ONE OF
    `section 5 does not apply`
    `construe to reflect the plain intention` HAS `of` IS A `Whose plain intention`
    `section 5 gives no direction because the plain intention cannot be ascertained`

DECLARE `The provision to be construed` HAS
    `where it is found`                                                IS A `Kind of enactment`
    `it relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is obscure or ambiguous`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a literal interpretation it would be absurd`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a literal interpretation it would fail to reflect the plain intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the plain intention can be ascertained`                           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:109 | Construing ambiguous or obscure provisions, etc. 5.—(1) In construing a provision of any Act (other than a provision that relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction)—
-- src:110 | (a) that is obscure or ambiguous, or
-- src:111 | (b) that on a literal interpretation would be absurd or would fail to reflect the plain intention of—
-- src:112 | (i) in the case of an Act to which paragraph (a) of the definition of “Act” in section 2 (1) relates, the Oireachtas, or
-- src:113 | (ii) in the case of an Act to which paragraph (b) of that definition relates, the parliament concerned,
-- src:114 | the provision shall be given a construction that reflects the plain intention of the Oireachtas or parliament concerned, as the case may be, where that intention can be ascertained from the Act as a whole.
-- src:115 | (2) In construing a provision of a statutory instrument (other than a provision that relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction)—
-- src:116 | (a) that is obscure or ambiguous, or
-- src:117 | (b) that on a literal interpretation would be absurd or would fail to reflect the plain intention of the instrument as a whole in the context of the enactment (including the Act) under which it was made,
-- src:118 | the provision shall be given a construction that reflects the plain intention of the maker of the instrument where that intention can be ascertained from the instrument as a whole in the context of that enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 5(1), (2) (src:109-118)
GIVEN p IS A `The provision to be construed`
GIVETH A `What section 5 directs`
`what section 5 directs about` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF p's `it relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction` THEN `section 5 does not apply`
           IF NOT (   p's `it is obscure or ambiguous`
                   OR p's `on a literal interpretation it would be absurd`
                   OR p's `on a literal interpretation it would fail to reflect the plain intention`)
              THEN `section 5 does not apply`
           IF NOT p's `the plain intention can be ascertained`
              THEN `section 5 gives no direction because the plain intention cannot be ascertained`
           OTHERWISE
              CONSIDER p's `where it is found`
              WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`                           THEN `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
              WHEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`   THEN `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the parliament concerned`
              WHEN `a statutory instrument`                             THEN `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the maker of the instrument`

§ `Section 6: construing a provision in changing circumstances`

DECLARE `A change since a provision was made` HAS
    `the day the Act was passed or the instrument was made`   IS A DATE
    `the day of the change`                                   IS A DATE
    `the change is in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used, or another relevant matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the text, purpose and context of the provision permit the allowance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:119 | Construing provisions in changing circumstances. 6.—In construing a provision of any Act or statutory instrument, a court may make allowances for any changes in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used in that Act or statutory instrument and other relevant matters, which have occurred since the date of the passing of that Act or the making of that statutory instrument, but only in so far as its text, purpose and context permit.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 6 (src:119)
GIVEN c IS A `A change since a provision was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT c's `the change is in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used, or another relevant matter` THEN FALSE
           IF NOT c's `the text, purpose and context of the provision permit the allowance` THEN FALSE
           IF c's `the day of the change` GREATER THAN c's `the day the Act was passed or the instrument was made` THEN TRUE
           IF c's `the day of the change` LESS THAN c's `the day the Act was passed or the instrument was made`    THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `section 6 does not say whether a change on the very day of the passing or making is a change since that day`

§ `Section 7: matters that accompany the signed text of an Act`

-- src:120 | Supplemental provision to sections 5 and 6. 7.—(1) In construing a provision of an Act for the purposes of section 5 or 6 , a court may, notwithstanding section 18 (g), make use of all matters that accompany and are set out in—
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1) (src:120)
GIVEN `where it is found`                                        IS A `Kind of enactment`
      `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `where it is found` `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where it is found`
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`                         THEN `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` AND `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`
    WHEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` THEN `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` AND `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`
    WHEN `a statutory instrument`                           THEN FALSE

-- src:124 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), it shall be presumed, until the contrary is shown, that a copy of the text of an Act that is required to be judicially noticed is a copy of the text to which subsection (1) relates.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(2) (src:124)
GIVEN `the copy is of the text of an Act that is required to be judicially noticed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` `the copy is of the text of an Act that is required to be judicially noticed` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    `the copy is of the text of an Act that is required to be judicially noticed` AND NOT `the contrary is shown`

§ `Section 8: reading provisions together as one and summary proceedings for offences`

DECLARE `Facts for section 8` HAS
    `the first Act or portion of an Act provides that summary proceedings for offences under it may be prosecuted by a specified person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is subsequently read together as one with a provision of another Act`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `an offence is created under that provision which can be prosecuted in a summary manner`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `no express power is given to the specified person to so prosecute`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:125 | Reading provisions together as one and summary proceedings for offences. 8.—Where—
-- src:126 | (a) an Act or portion of an Act (whenever passed)—
-- src:127 | (i) provides that summary proceedings for offences under it may be prosecuted by a specified person, and
-- src:128 | (ii) is subsequently read together as one with any provision of another Act,
-- src:129 | and
-- src:130 | (b) an offence is created under that provision which can be prosecuted in a summary manner but no express power is given to the specified person to so prosecute,
-- src:131 | then, the specified person may bring summary proceedings for an offence under that other provision unless some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 8 (src:125-131)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` f MEANS
        f's `the first Act or portion of an Act provides that summary proceedings for offences under it may be prosecuted by a specified person`
    AND f's `it is subsequently read together as one with a provision of another Act`
    AND f's `an offence is created under that provision which can be prosecuted in a summary manner`
    AND f's `no express power is given to the specified person to so prosecute`
    AND NOT f's `some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings`

§ `Section 9: references in enactments to Parts, subsections and the like`

DECLARE `A division named in a reference` IS ONE OF
    Part
    Chapter
    section
    Schedule
    subsection
    paragraph
    subparagraph
    clause
    subclause
    article
    subarticle
    `a division with another name`

DECLARE `What a reference is read as a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
    `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`

-- src:132 | References in enactments to Parts, etc. 9.—(1) A reference in an enactment to a Part, Chapter, section, Schedule or other division, by whatever name called, shall be read as a reference to a Part, Chapter, section, Schedule or other division of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
-- src:133 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause, article, subarticle or other division, by whatever name called, shall be read as a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause, article, subarticle or other division of the provision in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 9(1), (2) (src:132-133)
GIVEN d IS A `A division named in a reference`
GIVETH A `What a reference is read as a reference to`
`a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN Part                          THEN `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN Chapter                       THEN `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN section                       THEN `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN Schedule                      THEN `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN subsection                    THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN paragraph                     THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN subparagraph                  THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN clause                        THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN subclause                     THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN article                       THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN subarticle                    THEN `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    WHEN `a division with another name` THEN `section 9 does not say which kind of division a division with another name is`

§ `Section 11: examples`

DECLARE `A heading over an example` IS ONE OF
    Sampla
    Samplai
    Example
    Examples
    `some other heading`

DECLARE `The effect of an example` IS ONE OF
    `section 11 does not apply`
    `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`

-- src:135 | References in enactments to examples. 11.—If under the heading—
-- src:136 | (a) in the Irish language “Sampla” or “Samplaí”, or
-- src:137 | (b) in the English language “Example” or “Examples”,
-- src:138 | an enactment includes at the end of a provision or in a schedule relating to such provision an example of the operation of the provision, then the example—
-- src:139 | (i) is not to be read as exhaustive of the provision, and
-- src:140 | (ii) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the provision.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 11 (src:135-140)
GIVEN h IS A `A heading over an example`
      `it is included at the end of a provision or in a schedule relating to such provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The effect of an example`
`the effect of an example under the heading` h `, included as stated by` `it is included at the end of a provision or in a schedule relating to such provision` MEANS
    IF   `it is included at the end of a provision or in a schedule relating to such provision` AND `the heading is one the section names` h
    THEN `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
    ELSE `section 11 does not apply`

-- src:136 | (a) in the Irish language “Sampla” or “Samplaí”, or
-- src:137 | (b) in the English language “Example” or “Examples”,
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 11(a), (b) (src:136-137)
GIVEN h IS A `A heading over an example`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the heading is one the section names` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN Sampla             THEN TRUE
    WHEN Samplai            THEN TRUE
    WHEN Example            THEN TRUE
    WHEN Examples           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other heading` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 12: deviation from a prescribed form`

-- src:141 | Deviation from form. 12.—Where a form is prescribed in or under an enactment, a deviation from the form which does not materially affect the substance of the form or is not misleading in content or effect does not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 12 (src:141)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed in or under an enactment`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation does not materially affect the substance of the form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation is not misleading in content or effect`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 12 saves the form used` `a form is prescribed in or under an enactment` `the deviation does not materially affect the substance of the form` `the deviation is not misleading in content or effect` MEANS
        `a form is prescribed in or under an enactment`
    AND (   `the deviation does not materially affect the substance of the form`
         OR `the deviation is not misleading in content or effect`)

§ `Section 13: judicial notice`

-- src:143 | Judicial notice. 13.—An Act is a public document and shall be judicially noticed.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 13 (src:143)
GIVEN `where it is found` IS A `Kind of enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a public document that shall be judicially noticed` `where it is found` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where it is found`
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument`                           THEN `section 13 says nothing about a statutory instrument`

§ `Section 14(1): how an Act may be cited`

DECLARE `A way of citing an Act` IS ONE OF
    `by the long title`
    `by the short title`
    `by the consecutive number of the Act in the calendar year and the calendar year in which it was passed`
    `by its regnal year and chapter number`
    `by its regnal year, chapter number and the session concerned`

DECLARE `Facts about an Act for citing it` HAS
    `citing it by number and year is appropriate`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstat Eireann) Act 1922` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:144 | Citation and references to amended enactments. 14.—(1) An Act may be cited in any enactment or other document—
-- src:145 | (a) by the long title or short title of the Act,
-- src:146 | (b) where appropriate, by the consecutive number of the Act in the calendar year and by the calendar year in which it was passed, or
-- src:147 | (c) where the Act was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstát Eireann) Act 1922, by its regnal year and chapter number and, where there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year, by reference to the session concerned.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 14(1) (src:144-147)
GIVEN way IS A `A way of citing an Act`
      act IS A `Facts about an Act for citing it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14(1) lets an Act be cited` way `, given` act MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `by the long title`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by the short title` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by the consecutive number of the Act in the calendar year and the calendar year in which it was passed`
         THEN act's `citing it by number and year is appropriate`
    WHEN `by its regnal year and chapter number`
         THEN     act's `it was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstat Eireann) Act 1922`
              AND NOT act's `there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year`
    WHEN `by its regnal year, chapter number and the session concerned`
         THEN     act's `it was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstat Eireann) Act 1922`
              AND act's `there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year`
